<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patches>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       THE ALTAR'S GRANT PATH

       The altar is given, never built. Until now nothing gave it: no
       ScenPart, no quest node, no reward. This file is that path.

       It works by adding things to the site maps VQE Ancients generates for
       its Ancient Lab chain. Those maps are the only place the chain pays
       out at all. There is no reward node anywhere in that questline
       (verified: all six quest roots are C# QuestNode_Root_* that call
       GenerateSite and attach QuestPart_AncientLab, which ends the quest on
       a MinifyUtility.Uninstall signal). The "reward" is literally furniture
       standing on the generated map that you claim, uninstall and haul home.

       So spawnThings IS the extension point. StructureSetGenerator.
       SpawnPawnsAndThings calls ThingMaker.MakeThing(def, null) then
       GenSpawn.Spawn with zero eligibility filtering, and every VQEA lab
       facility inherits minifiedDef MinifiedThing plus claimable. So does
       Archinity_Altar.

       WHY THIS ADDS ALL TWELVE FACILITIES, NOT JUST THE ALTAR

       QuestPart_AncientLab ends each chain quest on the FIRST uninstall of
       the matching def, so the chain hands over roughly one facility per
       quest across five or six quests. The altar's
       CompProperties_AffectedByFacilities links twelve. Without this file
       most of the altar's facility rack would be permanently unobtainable.

       ON MULTIPLAYER

       This is generation-side only and it is safe. StructureSetGenerator
       runs inside map generation, which RimWorld executes under a seeded
       Rand state (GenStep_AncientComplex.SeedPart is 987654321). Adding
       entries shifts RNG consumption for that map, but shifts it
       identically on every client, because Multiplayer enforces a matching
       mod list and both clients therefore load byte-identical def XML.

       In shared mode there is one player faction and one colony, so one
       altar is both players' altar. Under multifaction this file becomes
       load-bearing rather than convenient: GameComponent_QuestChains has no
       faction dimension and fires the chain once for the whole game, so the
       second player gets nothing except what is spawned as ordinary loot.
       To double a payout, raise its count here. Nothing else changes.

       KNOWN COSMETIC COST

       The cell is chosen by CellFinder.RandomSpawnCellForPawnNear, which
       validates pawn standability, not a building footprint. Four of these
       facilities are 3x3 and the altar is 3x2, so one spawned against a
       vault wall will WipeMode.Vanish what it overlaps. Expect the
       occasional hole in a wall. Not a crash, not a desync.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Vanilla Quests Expanded - Ancients</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- The altar itself, on the first site in the chain, so it arrives
             as early as the chain can deliver it. One copy: it is a single
             shared building even under multifaction, because only one
             colony can hold it. -->
        <!-- expect: 1 -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/VanillaQuestsExpandedAncients.StructureSetDef[defName="VQEA_AncientLabComplexStructure"]/structureLayouts/li[pattern="VQEA_LabModules_1_.*"]/spawnThings</xpath>
          <value>
            <Archinity_Altar>1</Archinity_Altar>
            <VQEA_NeurostabilizerArray>1</VQEA_NeurostabilizerArray>
            <VQEA_RapidInfusionPump>1</VQEA_RapidInfusionPump>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- expect: 1 -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/VanillaQuestsExpandedAncients.StructureSetDef[defName="VQEA_ArchiteControlVaultStructure"]/structureLayouts/li[pattern="VQEA_LabModules_2_.*"]/spawnThings</xpath>
          <value>
            <VQEA_ArchiteRecycler>1</VQEA_ArchiteRecycler>
            <VQEA_GenomicAttenuator>1</VQEA_GenomicAttenuator>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- expect: 1 -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/VanillaQuestsExpandedAncients.StructureSetDef[defName="VQEA_SpliceframeBlacksiteStructure"]/structureLayouts/li[pattern="VQEA_LabModules_3_.*"]/spawnThings</xpath>
          <value>
            <VQEA_SpliceframeUplink>1</VQEA_SpliceframeUplink>
            <VQEA_RejectionBufferCoil>1</VQEA_RejectionBufferCoil>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- expect: 1 -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/VanillaQuestsExpandedAncients.StructureSetDef[defName="VQEA_InhibitorResearchLabStructure"]/structureLayouts/li[pattern="VQEA_LabModules_4_.*"]/spawnThings</xpath>
          <value>
            <VQEA_MutagenInhibitorCore>1</VQEA_MutagenInhibitorCore>
            <VQEA_TraitSelectionPrism>1</VQEA_TraitSelectionPrism>
            <VQEA_CognitiveRecoveryArray>1</VQEA_CognitiveRecoveryArray>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- expect: 1 -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/VanillaQuestsExpandedAncients.StructureSetDef[defName="VQEA_ArchiteArraySiteStructure"]/structureLayouts/li[pattern="VQEA_LabModules_5_.*"]/spawnThings</xpath>
          <value>
            <VQEA_ArchitePathingArray>1</VQEA_ArchitePathingArray>
            <VQEA_ComplexityHarmonizer>1</VQEA_ComplexityHarmonizer>
            <VQEA_AberrationRedirector>1</VQEA_AberrationRedirector>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- The research vault's li ships spawnPawns and no spawnThings at
             all, so this operation inserts the whole element rather than
             adding into one. Target is the li, not a child. -->
        <!-- expect: 1 -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/VanillaQuestsExpandedAncients.StructureSetDef[defName="VQEA_AncientResearchVaultStructure_Underground"]/structureLayouts/li[pattern="VQEA_SidequestLabModules_.*"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <spawnThings>
              <VQEA_NeurostabilizerArray>1</VQEA_NeurostabilizerArray>
            </spawnThings>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patches>
